        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(exec): require approval for OpenClaw lifecycle commands",
        "body": "﻿﻿﻿﻿Fixes #99518\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where exec commands through gateway or node hosts could let OpenClaw gateway/daemon lifecycle mutations pass through normal allowlist or auto-review paths when they should require explicit approval.\n\nThe affected workflow is OpenClaw self-management from exec surfaces: stopping, starting, restarting, running, deleting, or uninstalling the gateway/daemon through CLI, launchctl, systemctl, schtasks, process-kill, shell-wrapper, package-manager, Windows shim, `env -S`, `sudo`/`doas`, and dispatch-wrapper commands.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis adds a focused lifecycle classifier to the exec approval policy and wires it into both gateway-host and node-host approval analysis. The guard forces explicit approval for OpenClaw lifecycle mutations unless exec is already in yolo mode (`security=full`, `ask=off`).\n\nThe follow-up update also covers foreground gateway runtime forms that were missed by the first patch: `openclaw gateway`, `openclaw gateway run`, `openclaw gateway --force`, and option-only gateway run surfaces such as `--port`. Read-only gateway inspection remains outside the guard, including `openclaw gateway status`, `openclaw gateway call ...`, `openclaw gateway --help`, `openclaw gateway run --help`, `launchctl print`, `systemctl status`, `schtasks /Query`, and generic read-only process lookups.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators get an extra human confirmation before an agent or auto-review path can stop, start, restart, run, delete, or uninstall the OpenClaw gateway/daemon in non-yolo configurations. Existing yolo-mode behavior and read-only status/query commands are unchanged.\n\n## Evidence\n\nIssue review feedback incorporated: lifecycle classification now has regression coverage for the ordering invariant that classification happens before durable allowlist trust or auto-review decisions.\n\nLive gateway-host proof from an isolated branch gateway (`node scripts/run-node.mjs gateway run --port <random> --bind loopback --allow-unconfigured`, independent temp state/config):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"branchHead\": \"0ce214f5c1a1\",\n  \"isolatedGateway\": {\n    \"healthOk\": true\n  },\n  \"lifecycleAllowlistOnMissAutoReview\": {\n    \"command\": \"openclaw gateway --force\",\n    \"autoReviewCalls\": 0,\n    \"resultStatus\": \"approval-unavailable\",\n    \"hasLifecycleWarning\": true,\n    \"warningCount\": 1\n  },\n  \"yoloFullOff\": {\n    \"command\": \"openclaw gateway --force\",\n    \"allowedWithoutPending\": true,\n    \"warningCount\": 0\n  }\n}\n```\n\n`approval-unavailable` is expected in this isolated proof because no approval delivery route is configured; it is still a blocking approval result before command execution, and `autoReviewCalls: 0` proves the lifecycle command was not laundered through auto-review first. The `yoloFullOff` case confirms `security=full` + `ask=off` remains unchanged.\n\nFocused tests:\n\n```shell\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/infra/exec-approvals-policy.test.ts --testNamePattern=\"OpenClaw lifecycle|read-only or generic\"\n# Tests  136 passed | 111 skipped (247)\n\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/bash-tools.exec-host-gateway.test.ts --testNamePattern=\"OpenClaw lifecycle|durable allowlist\"\n# Tests  4 passed | 53 skipped (57)\n\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/bash-tools.exec-host-node.test.ts --testNamePattern=\"OpenClaw lifecycle\"\n# Tests  1 passed | 48 skipped (49)\n\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/node-host/invoke-system-run.test.ts --testNamePattern=\"OpenClaw lifecycle|empty env operands\"\n# Tests  2 passed | 33 skipped (35)\n```\n\nStatic checks:\n\n```shell\npnpm tsgo:prod\n# passed\n\npnpm exec oxlint src/infra/exec-approvals.ts src/infra/exec-approvals-policy.test.ts src/agents/bash-tools.exec-host-gateway.test.ts src/agents/bash-tools.exec-host-node.test.ts src/node-host/invoke-system-run.test.ts src/utils/shell-argv.ts src/utils/utils-misc.test.ts\n# passed\n\ngit diff --check\n# passed\n```\n\nAutoreview:\n\n```shell\npython .agents\\skills\\autoreview\\scripts\\autoreview --mode local --no-web-search --prompt \"Review the dirty OpenClaw PR #99530 follow-up patch...\"\n# attempted twice; no final clean result claimed\n```\n\nThe first helper run was interrupted by an outer 3-minute timeout. The second run used `--stream-engine-output` with a 30-minute timeout, but produced no structured reviewer output and left a stuck Codex reviewer process, which was cleaned up. Focused tests, static checks, and the isolated live gateway proof above are therefore the current validation for this update.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
        "branch": "fix/exec-approval-lifecycle-guard",
